Virtio MMIO transport (QEMU virt)
==================================

Thin register-layout wrapper over the memory-mapped virtio
transport the QEMU `virt` machine exposes at `0x0a000000`. QEMU
places 32 slots 0x200 bytes apart; a slot is "present" when its
`MagicValue` register reads as `'virt'` (little-endian
`0x74726976`). `DeviceID` (0=none, 1=net, 2=blk, ...) says what
device lives in the slot, if any.

This phase is a probe only — enough to enumerate the transports
at boot. The full virtio-net driver (virtqueue setup, TX/RX
rings, MSI/IRQ plumbing) lands in a later iteration on top of
this scaffold.

Follows **virtio-mmio v2** (modern). Legacy v1 isn't supported.

    module oskit.drivers.virtio


Transport region layout.

    val VIRTIO_MMIO_BASE: i64 = 0x0a000000
    val VIRTIO_MMIO_STRIDE: i64 = 0x200
    val VIRTIO_MMIO_MAX = 32


Register offsets. Every register is 4 bytes.

    val VIRTIO_REG_MAGIC      = 0x00
    val VIRTIO_REG_VERSION    = 0x04
    val VIRTIO_REG_DEVICE_ID  = 0x08
    val VIRTIO_REG_VENDOR_ID  = 0x0c
    val VIRTIO_REG_STATUS     = 0x70


Magic for present slots. Reads as the ASCII bytes `'v'`, `'i'`,
`'r'`, `'t'` in little-endian order.

    val VIRTIO_MMIO_MAGIC: i32 = 0x74726976


Device IDs we care about.

    val VIRTIO_DEV_NONE = 0
    val VIRTIO_DEV_NET  = 1
    val VIRTIO_DEV_BLK  = 2


MMIO read — every register on virtio-mmio is u32. Uses the same
raw-pointer cast pattern as the PL011 UART driver so the
compiler doesn't try to reorder the read.

    virtio_read32(base: i64, off: int) -> i32
        volatile var p: *i32 = *i32(base + i64(off))
        *p


Is the slot at `base` present? True when its magic reads as
`'virt'`.

    virtio_present(base: i64) -> int
        if virtio_read32(base, VIRTIO_REG_MAGIC) == VIRTIO_MMIO_MAGIC
            return 1
        0


`DeviceID` register: 0 if unused, otherwise a virtio device
type number (see the spec).

    virtio_device_id(base: i64) -> int
        int(virtio_read32(base, VIRTIO_REG_DEVICE_ID))


Walk all slots looking for the first one whose `DeviceID`
matches `dev_id`. Returns 0 when no slot matches.

    virtio_find(dev_id: int) -> i64
        var i = 0
        while i < VIRTIO_MMIO_MAX
            val base: i64 = VIRTIO_MMIO_BASE + i64(i) * VIRTIO_MMIO_STRIDE
            if virtio_present(base) != 0
                if virtio_device_id(base) == dev_id
                    return base
            i += 1
        0
